{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794561749437,"sessionID":"ses_e2bccb12cffeMW9EBW6csHr3DM","part":{"id":"prt_1d43731bd001Ut6Tt2Tpkjdjt0","sessionID":"ses_e2bccb12cffeMW9EBW6csHr3DM","messageID":"msg_1d436e2470019FvpIuSiylIcWR","type":"step-start","snapshot":"026a78fbfc020ff912fa935ac05877a50a4f0640"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794561749947,"sessionID":"ses_e2bccb12cffeMW9EBW6csHr3DM","part":{"partID":"prt_1d43731c30014Y4zAfgan6l56H","sessionID":"ses_e2bccb12cffeMW9EBW6csHr3DM","messageID":"msg_1d436e2470019FvpIuSiylIcWR","type":"tool","id":"call_df6aa29baf01402aa9c70843","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md","limit":80},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md, lines 1-80\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Rule: Evidence and proof\"\n3: description: \"A claim is only as strong as the observation behind it, and a receipt confirms only what could have contradicted it. Distinguish observed from derived from inferred.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"observed derived inferred\"\n6:   - \"how a green run lies\"\n7:   - \"exit 0 with no output\"\n8:   - \"negative control\"\n9:   - \"watch it fail first\"\n10:   - \"baseline before no regressions\"\n11:   - \"a finding is a hypothesis\"\n12:   - \"the sub-agent said complete\"\n13:   - \"the tool reported success\"\n14:   - \"claiming done\"\n15:   - \"final-state proof\"\n16:   - \"proof plan before implementation\"\n17:   - \"reason from data not memory\"\n18:   - \"the doc disagrees with the code\"\n19:   - \"honest close-out\"\n20:   - \"committed pushed dirty\"\n21:   - \"what only the operator can verify\"\n22:   - \"unconfirmed cause\"\n23:   - \"suspected cause\"\n24:   - \"cause then fix\"\n25:   - \"tests pass\"\n26:   - \"verify before claiming done\"\n27: importance_tier: important\n28: contextType: reference\n29: version: 1.1.1.6\n30: ---\n31: \n32: # Rule: Evidence and proof\n33: \n34: > Routed from [`REPO RULES.md`](../../REPO%20RULES.md). Load before making any claim someone will act on.\n35: > Expands `AGENTS.md`, never overrides it. Where they appear to disagree, `AGENTS.md` wins and this file is wrong. Say so.\n36: \n37: ## Fires when\n38: \n39: - About to say \"done\", \"complete\", \"works\", \"fixed\", \"passing\", or \"no regressions\".\n40: - About to report a result, a number, a file path, or command output.\n41: - A tool, sub-agent, or reviewer reports success or a finding and you are about to act on it.\n42: - About to write a completion summary, or tick anything off as done.\n43: - You are closing out a turn.\n44: \n45: ## The rule\n46: \n47: **A claim is only as strong as the observation behind it. Every load-bearing claim\n48: carries its receipt, or is explicitly labeled as inferred.**\n49: \n50: ---\n51: \n52: ## 1. THREE TIERS\n53: \n54: | Tier | Meaning | How it must appear |\n55: |------|---------|--------------------|\n56: | **OBSERVED** | You ran it and read the output and exit status | Cite the receipt: the command, the `file:line`, the artifact path |\n57: | **DERIVED** | Follows necessarily from something observed | Show the observation and the step from it |\n58: | **INFERRED** | Plausible, unverified | Say so, and say what would confirm it |\n59: \n60: Prose that mixes the three without marking them reads as if all of it were observed.\n61: What to do when a claim cannot be resolved is\n62: [`uncertainty-and-honesty.md`](uncertainty-and-honesty.md).\n63: \n64: **A receipt confirms only what could have contradicted it.** If the claim being false would\n65: have left the receipt unchanged, the receipt is not an observation of that claim. It\n66: belongs in INFERRED until repaired. Four shapes recur, each with one repair.\n67: A search that found nothing: demonstrate the search on a known instance of what you claim\n68: is absent, or you have tested your pattern, not the claim. A read that stopped short: read\n69: the span where the failure would actually print. A total carried from another analysis:\n70: derive it here, at the total's own level. A match that never distinguished roles: compare\n71: what the two sides are, not the digits they share. With no known instance to hand, the\n72: honest output is INFERRED plus the step that would confirm it.\n73: \n74: When a report leads with a cause, the cause carries its standing, and the cause-then-fix\n75: order holds. Where no run confirms the cause, it is INFERRED: label it as suspected and\n76: name the next check. A confirmed cause is reported as a finding with its receipt. There\n77: is no unmarked case.\n78: \n79: The failure this prevents: an unconfirmed cause asserted as definitive, which the next\n80: reader treats as settled and stops testing.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 81]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md, lines 1-80\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Rule: Evidence and proof\"\n3: description: \"A claim is only as strong as the observation behind it, and a receipt confirms only what could have contradicted it. Distinguish observed from derived from inferred.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"observed derived inferred\"\n6:   - \"how a green run lies\"\n7:   - \"exit 0 with no output\"\n8:   - \"negative control\"\n9:   - \"watch it fail first\"\n10:   - \"baseline before no regressions\"\n11:   - \"a finding is a hypothesis\"\n12:   - \"the sub-agent said complete\"\n13:   - \"the tool reported success\"\n14:   - \"claiming done\"\n15:   - \"final-state proof\"\n16:   - \"proof plan before implementation\"\n17:   - \"reason from data not memory\"\n18:   - \"the doc disagrees with the code\"\n19:   - \"honest close-out\"\n20:   - \"committed pushed dirty\"\n21:   - \"what only the operator can verify\"\n22:   - \"unconfirmed cause\"\n23:   - \"suspected cause\"\n24:   - \"cause then fix\"\n25:   - \"tests pass\"\n26:   - \"verify before claiming done\"\n27: importance_tier: important\n28: contextType: reference\n29: version: 1.1.1.6\n30: ---\n31: \n32: # Rule: Evidence and proof\n33: \n34: > Routed from [`REPO RULES.md`](../../REPO%20RULES.md). Load before making any claim someone will act on.\n35: > Expands `AGENTS.md`, never overrides it. Where they appear to disagree, `AGENTS.md` wins and this file is wrong. Say so.\n36: \n37: ## Fires when\n38: \n39: - About to say \"done\", \"complete\", \"works\", \"fixed\", \"passing\", or \"no regressions\".\n40: - About to report a result, a number, a file path, or command output.\n41: - A tool, sub-agent, or reviewer reports success or a finding and you are about to act on it.\n42: - About to write a completion summary, or tick anything off as done.\n43: - You are closing out a turn.\n44: \n45: ## The rule\n46: \n47: **A claim is only as strong as the observation behind it. Every load-bearing claim\n48: carries its receipt, or is explicitly labeled as inferred.**\n49: \n50: ---\n51: \n52: ## 1. THREE TIERS\n53: \n54: | Tier | Meaning | How it must appear |\n55: |------|---------|--------------------|\n56: | **OBSERVED** | You ran it and read the output and exit status | Cite the receipt: the command, the `file:line`, the artifact path |\n57: | **DERIVED** | Follows necessarily from something observed | Show the observation and the step from it |\n58: | **INFERRED** | Plausible, unverified | Say so, and say what would confirm it |\n59: \n60: Prose that mixes the three without marking them reads as if all of it were observed.\n61: What to do when a claim cannot be resolved is\n62: [`uncertainty-and-honesty.md`](uncertainty-and-honesty.md).\n63: \n64: **A receipt confirms only what could have contradicted it.** If the claim being false would\n65: have left the receipt unchanged, the receipt is not an observation of that claim. It\n66: belongs in INFERRED until repaired. Four shapes recur, each with one repair.\n67: A search that found nothing: demonstrate the search on a known instance of what you claim\n68: is absent, or you have tested your pattern, not the claim. A read that stopped short: read\n69: the span where the failure would actually print. A total carried from another analysis:\n70: derive it here, at the total's own level. A match that never distinguished roles: compare\n71: what the two sides are, not the digits they share. With no known instance to hand, the\n72: honest output is INFERRED plus the step that would confirm it.\n73: \n74: When a report leads with a cause, the cause carries its standing, and the cause-then-fix\n75: order holds. Where no run confirms the cause, it is INFERRED: label it as suspected and\n76: name the next check. A confirmed cause is reported as a finding with its receipt. There\n77: is no unmarked case.\n78: \n79: The failure this prevents: an unconfirmed cause asserted as definitive, which the next\n80: reader treats as settled and stops testing.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 81]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md\",\"limit\":80}"},"time":{"start":1794561749443,"end":1794561749947}}}}
